<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Suriagehara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1589</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Suriagehara was fought in 1589 near Mount Bandai in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune">Date Masamune</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a> Yoshihiro. Masamune's victory destroyed the power of the Ashina and gave him their castle and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> region, making the Date the dominant clan of southern Tohoku. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, who had forbidden private wars, took Aizu from him in 1590.</p></div>
